        <description>Cuts of meat from the short loin of a muffalo, including the titular T-shaped bone.\n\n&lt;color=#6e6e6eff&gt;On the rim, settlers favor the t-bone as a cut with both delicate meat on one side, and beefier flesh on the other. This duality is seen as a metaphor for life on rimworlds: tender, yet tough.&lt;/color&gt;</description>
