    <ThingDef ParentName="OrganicProductBase">
        <defName>SC_ThrumboRib</defName>
        <label>thrumbo rib</label>
        <description>The large ribs of a graceful thrumbo, separated into single chops.\n\n&lt;color=#6e6e6eff&gt;Traditionally, tribal societies surround thrumbos in folklore and myth, thus their flesh is only eaten upon the natural passing of the animal. This ritual feast can last up to a week, in which the tribe will eat every piece of the thrumbo: after grand dances and celebrations, an honorable burial is held for the clean skeleton of the animal.&lt;/color&gt;</description>
